    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/potato.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">potato</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/onion.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">onion</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cucumber.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cucumber</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/broccoli.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">broccoli</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mushroom.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mushroom</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/meat.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">meat</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pasta.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">pasta</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pizza.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">pizza</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hamburger.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hamburger</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fries.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">french fries</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/soup.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">soup</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cake.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cake</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cookie.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cookie</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/chocolate.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">chocolate</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/ice-cream.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">ice cream</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/juice.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">juice</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/beer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">beer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/wine.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">wine</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/soda.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">soda</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read the cafe order</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Good morning. I'd like <strong>a sandwich</strong> and <strong>an apple</strong>, please. And can I have <strong>some water</strong> and <strong>a coffee</strong>? — Sorry, we don't have <strong>any juice</strong> today."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">a sandwich</span> and <span class="ex">an apple</span>. Both mean <strong>one</strong> item you can count. Why is one <span class="ex">a</span> and the other <span class="ex">an</span>?</li>
      <li>Now look at <span class="ex">some water</span>. Why don't we say <span class="ex">a water</span>? Can you count water the way you count sandwiches?</li>
      <li>The cafe says <span class="ex">we don't have any juice</span>. In this <strong>negative</strong> sentence, which little word replaces <span class="ex">some</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — read the cue, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">If you can count it (one item), use <b>a / an</b>. If it's an amount, use <b>some</b>. Choose <b>an</b> before a, e, i, o, u sounds.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="some">some</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I'd like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sandwich. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one item · count it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Can I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> apple? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one item · starts with a vowel sound)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I'd like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> water. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(an amount · can't count it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Can I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> rice? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(an amount · can't count it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: count it or measure it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Some foods come in <strong>single items you can count</strong>: <span class="ex">one apple, two apples, three eggs</span>. We call these <strong>countable</strong>. Use <span class="ex">a / an</span> for one of them.</p>
  <p>Other foods are an <strong>amount or mass you don't count one by one</strong>: <span class="ex">water, rice, cheese, bread</span>. We call these <strong>uncountable</strong>. Use <span class="ex">some</span> for an amount, not <span class="ex">a / an</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>countable <span class="contraction">use a / an</span></th><th>uncountable <span class="contraction">use some</span></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>a sandwich</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">one, two sandwiches</span></td><td><b>some bread</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not a bread</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>an apple</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">one, two apples</span></td><td><b>some rice</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not a rice</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>an egg</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">one, two eggs</span></td><td><b>some water</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not a water</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a coffee</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">= one cup, in a cafe</span></td><td><b>some cheese</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not a cheese</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Why <span class="ex">an apple</span> but <span class="ex">a sandwich</span>? Use <span class="ex">an</span> before a vowel sound: <span class="ex">an apple, an egg, an orange</span>. Use <span class="ex">a</span> before a consonant sound: <span class="ex">a sandwich, a coffee, a banana</span>.</li>
      <li>Use <span class="ex">any</span> in most neutral questions and negatives: <span class="ex">Is there any milk? There isn't any juice.</span> In offers and requests, <span class="ex">some</span> is common: <span class="ex">Would you like some coffee? Can I have some water?</span></li>
      <li>In a cafe we can say <span class="ex">a coffee</span> or <span class="ex">a water</span> to mean <strong>one cup / one bottle</strong>. But to talk about the drink in general, use <span class="ex">some water</span>, <span class="ex">some coffee</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>some / any in statements, questions, and negatives</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Use <span class="ex">some</span> in plain statements. Use <span class="ex">any</span> in most neutral questions and negatives:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">There is <strong>some</strong> milk. &nbsp; · &nbsp; Is there <strong>any</strong> milk? &nbsp; · &nbsp; There isn't <strong>any</strong> milk.</span></p>
  <p>In offers and requests, use <span class="ex">some</span> when you are offering something or asking for an amount: <span class="ex">Would you like <strong>some</strong> coffee? Can I have <strong>some</strong> water?</span></p>
  <p>And remember the verb: one uncountable amount takes <span class="ex">is</span>; plural countable items take <span class="ex">are</span>: <span class="ex">There is some rice. There are some apples.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1 — choose some or any</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Statement, offer, or request → usually <b>some</b>. Neutral question or negative → usually <b>any</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="some">some</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="any">any</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>There is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> bread on the table. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(statement)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Can I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose" data-hint="This is a request for an amount, so use some." data-fix="some">choose</button> coffee, please? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(request)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Sorry, we don't have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="any" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> juice today. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(negative)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I bought <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> vegetables at the market. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(statement)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Do we need <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="any" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> milk for breakfast? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(question)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>There aren't <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="any" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> eggs in the fridge. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(negative)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Would you like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> fruit? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(offer)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 2 — sort each food: countable or uncountable?</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a food word, then tap the box where it belongs</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="apple">apple</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="water">water</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="egg">egg</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="rice">rice</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="sandwich">sandwich</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="cheese">cheese</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="apple" data-placeholder="countable · one apple, two apples">countable · one apple, two apples</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="egg" data-placeholder="countable · one egg, two eggs">countable · one egg, two eggs</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="sandwich" data-placeholder="countable · one sandwich, two sandwiches">countable · one sandwich, two sandwiches</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="water" data-placeholder="uncountable · some water, not a water">uncountable · some water, not a water</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="rice" data-placeholder="uncountable · some rice, not a rice">uncountable · some rice, not a rice</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="cheese" data-placeholder="uncountable · some cheese, not a cheese">uncountable · some cheese, not a cheese</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i'd like a coffee">
    <h3>Drill 3 — build the order</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You want one cup of coffee in a cafe. Build the polite order, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="coffee">coffee</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i'd">I'd</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="like">like</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there is some bread">
    <h3>Drill 4 — build the sentence with an amount</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Bread is uncountable, so use <span class="ex">is</span> and <span class="ex">some</span>. Build the sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="bread">bread</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="some">some</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="a" data-fix="Can I have some rice?" data-why="Rice is uncountable, so we don't use a. Use some for an amount: some rice.">
    <h3>Drill 5 — count it or not?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. <span class="ex">Rice</span> is an amount, not a single item.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="can">Can</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">a</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rice">rice?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-fix="There are some apples." data-why="Apples is plural and countable, so the verb is are, not is. There are some apples.">
    <h3>Drill 6 — match the verb to the food</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. <span class="ex">Apples</span> are countable and plural.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there">There</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="some">some</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="apples">apples.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 — add the right word, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the new phrase aloud first, choosing <span class="ex">a</span>, <span class="ex">an</span>, or <span class="ex">some</span>. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> apple &nbsp;→&nbsp; one item (count it)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>an apple</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> water &nbsp;→&nbsp; an amount</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>some water</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> sandwich &nbsp;→&nbsp; one item (count it)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>a sandwich</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> cheese &nbsp;→&nbsp; an amount</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>some cheese</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> There is some milk. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it a question</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Is there any milk?</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A lunch order</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Lunch order for the office: two chicken sandwiches, one green salad, and a bowl of rice. For drinks, three coffees and a bottle of water. No milk in one of the coffees, please.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real food order.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. How many sandwiches are in the order?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two">two</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="one">one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="coffee and water">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What are the drinks?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="coffee and water">coffee and water</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="tea and milk">tea and milk</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="juice and water">juice and water</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="milk">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What does one coffee not have?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="milk">milk</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sugar">sugar</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="water">water</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Order in a cafe:</b> Role-play with the teacher. The teacher is the server. Order food and a drink politely. <span class="ex">I'd like a sandwich and an apple, please. Can I have some water?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Take the order:</b> Now you are the server. Ask and respond. <span class="ex">Hi, would you like a coffee or some tea? — Sorry, we don't have any juice today.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your three meals:</b> Say what you usually eat and drink. <span class="ex">For breakfast I have some bread and a coffee. For lunch I have a salad. For dinner I have some rice and chicken.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Likes and dislikes:</b> Name foods you like and don't like, in full sentences. <span class="ex">I like fish and vegetables. I don't like soup. I really like fruit.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Check the fridge:</b> Look in your fridge (real or imagined) and report. <span class="ex">There is some cheese and some milk. There are some eggs. There isn't any juice.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For one item I can count, I use <strong>a</strong> or <strong>an</strong>. For an amount in a statement, offer, or request, I often use ______. In most neutral questions and negatives, I use ______. I use <strong>an</strong> before a ______ sound.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about what you eat for breakfast and one about a food you don't like.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can name everyday foods and drinks and choose a, an, some, or any in statements, neutral questions, negatives, offers, and requests.">
    <h3>Final quiz — choose the right word</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="an">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. I'd like ___ egg for breakfast.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="some">some</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="some">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Can I have ___ water, please?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="some">some</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. She is eating ___ sandwich.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="some">some</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="any">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Is there ___ milk in the fridge?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="some">some</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="any">any</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="any">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Sorry, we don't have ___ juice today.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="some">some</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="any">any</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="uncountable">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which word is uncountable (use <em>some</em>, not <em>a</em>)?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="countable">apple</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="uncountable">rice</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="countable2">sandwich</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There are some apples.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are some apples.">There are some apples.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is some apples.">There is some apples.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are a apples.">There are a apples.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I'd like some coffee.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. You want coffee in general (not one cup). Which is best?</p>
